post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

steel-apparmor: AppArmor is NOT active until the kernel is told to enable it.

  Arch builds AppArmor into the kernel but does not select it, so installing
  the package alone changes nothing. Add this to your kernel command line and
  reboot:

      lsm=landlock,lockdown,yama,integrity,apparmor apparmor=1 security=apparmor

  The full fragment is at /usr/share/steel-apparmor/cmdline. Note that the
  lsm= list must be complete — naming only apparmor silently disables
  landlock, lockdown, yama, and integrity.

  On an image deployment this is baked into the signed UKI and you do not
  have to do anything.

  Then:

      systemctl enable --now apparmor.service
      steel-profile status

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  systemctl is-active --quiet apparmor.service && systemctl reload apparmor.service || true
}
